From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jake Cattrall <krazyjakee@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 03:09:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fill edge-to-edge tiles of an axis-aligned linear gradient in
 one go

A linear gradient whose line runs edge to edge of its tile along one axis,
over tiles laid without gaps (a grid of lines, stripes), is drawn as one
fill of the tiled area with the gradient repeating, instead of a fill per
tile. That draws the same pixels, costs one fill instead of hundreds, and
no longer runs into the 500-tile limit, past which such backgrounds (a
48px grid over a 1440x900 window) were not drawn at all.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
